--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
CableDyn input file: IEA-15MW on the UMaine VolturnUS-S with lines 1 and 2 hung from the two ends
of a Coupled pontoon rod (100 m, 1 m diameter) that runs between their fairleads (OpenFAST,
CompMooring = 5). The rod is a node of the coupling mesh at its End A: it follows the platform
position and orientation and returns the force and moment of its lines, weight, buoyancy,
Morison loads, and inertia. Line 3 stays on a Coupled point. MoorDyn_UMaine_rod.dat is the stock
MoorDyn twin used for the coupled-rod comparison in validation/OPENFAST_DLC_VERIFICATION.md.
